Termux private storage and Android shared storage are separate. You need to explicitly copy or move files between them.

To copy from Termux to Android: {{command}}cp ~/file.txt ~/storage/shared/Documents/{{/command}}

To copy from Android to Termux: {{command}}cp ~/storage/shared/Download/document.pdf ~/{{/command}}

Use {{command}}-r{{/command}} to copy entire folders (recursive). Use {{command}}mv{{/command}} instead of {{command}}cp{{/command}} if you want to move (rather than copy) the file.

SCP and Rsync use SSH to transfer files securely. SCP is simple and works like cp. Rsync is more efficient for large transfers.

SCP syntax: {{command}}scp -P 8022 username@phone_ip:~/file.txt ./{{/command}} copies from phone to computer.

Rsync is better for syncing folders: {{command}}rsync -avz -e 'ssh -p 8022' username@phone_ip:~/documents/ ./backup/{{/command}}

Use SSH to access Termux remotely from your computer over WiFi.

On your phone, install openssh and start the server with {{command}}sshd{{/command}}. Find your phone's IP address with {{command}}ifconfig{{/command}}.

On your computer, connect with {{command}}ssh -p 8022 username@phone_ip{{/command}}. Transfer files with {{command}}scp -P 8022 file.txt username@phone_ip:~/.{{/command}}
